engine/science.md adapts the paper-review prompt of Liang et al., "Can large language
models provide useful feedback on research papers? A large-scale empirical analysis"
(arXiv:2310.01783), as distributed in Allen AI's marg-reviewer repository, and adds the
claims-to-experiments method of MARG (D'Arcy et al., "MARG: Multi-Agent Review Generation
for Scientific Papers", arXiv:2401.04259) and a condensed matter checklist.
engine/merge.md is original to this project.

research/ holds the evaluation behind the plugin. research/eval/referee/*/referee.json and
the referee reports quoted in research/eval/ contain excerpts of published peer review files
from Nature, Nature Communications, Nature Physics and Communications Materials, and of
SciPost Physics reports. These are published under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Credit: Anonymous
Referee(s), in the peer review file of each article; each paper's arXiv ID, DOI and
peer-review source URL are listed in research/eval/referee/pool.json, papers.json and
candidates.json. The excerpts are shortened and summarized, which is a change from the original.

The AI reviews in research/ quote short passages from the arXiv preprints they review,
identified by arXiv ID, for the purpose of review and evaluation.
